    <section id="sobre">

        <h2>About Us</h2>

        <h3>Eduarda</h3>

        <h4>Birth</h4>

        <p>
            Eduarda was born on the morning of June 14, 2010, a
            Monday, in Umuarama-PR, at the Nossa Senhora Aparecida Hospital.
            I remember the doctors were betting on how much she would weigh —
            the one who guessed over 3kg was right! It was a very emotional day, full of
            joy for the whole family.
        </p>


        <h4>Educational Background</h4>

        <p>
            My educational journey began in Céu Azul, at São
            Cristóvão School, where I studied from the 1st to the 5th grade. Later, I moved to
            Nova Santa Rosa and continued my studies at Marechal Gaspar Dutra
            State College, where I completed my middle school education.
            Currently, I am in the 1st year of high school at IFPR in Toledo,
            in a new phase of my school life. Changing schools
            brought new challenges and experiences, contributing to my
            growth and the construction of my path so far.
        </p>


        <h4>Historical Fact:</h4>

        <p>
            A landmark event of 2010 was the World Cup,
            held in South Africa between June and July of that year.
            It was the first time the African continent hosted a World
            Cup. The Spanish national team was the champion, winning its
            first world title after defeating the Netherlands in the final.
        </p>


        <h4>Current Moment:</h4>

        <p>
            Currently, I am in the 1st year of high school at IFPR,
            which has been a huge privilege. I am discovering new
            interests, learning new things, and thinking more and more
            about my future.
        </p>


        <h4>Future Perspectives:</h4>

        <p>
            I wish to finish high school and then enter a
            college in the field of Marketing. I intend to specialize in this
            area and build a career that allows me to work with
            creativity and what I love.
        </p>

    </section>


    <section id="onde-vivemos">

        <h2>Where We Live</h2>

        <h4>Municipality - Nova Santa Rosa:</h4>

        <p>
            Nova Santa Rosa is a municipality located in western Paraná and
            has a history marked by the colonization of families who came
            mainly from Rio Grande do Sul, many of them of Germanic
            origin. Colonization began in 1953 and the municipality
            achieved its political-administrative emancipation in 1976.
            One of the cultural characteristics of the municipality is the German influence,
            present in customs, traditions, and even the language, which is still
            preserved by some families. Nova Santa Rosa also has the Dom Severino Kögl
            Municipal Museum, created to preserve objects, photographs,
            and documents related to the history of the early settlers.
        </p>


        <h4>Neighborhood</h4>

        <p>
            I live in the Cidade Nova neighborhood. It is a quiet region of Nova Santa Rosa,
            consisting mainly of houses and residential streets. It is a simple neighborhood,
            where many people know each other and interact day by day.
        </p>

    </section>


